WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Some questions have a list of fixed answers, like the location or

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.600
type of work, or it could be a fire risk assessment that might be

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.380
graded as trivial, tolerable and so on.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.300
To do that we can set the answer type to graded, then choose the

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.800
words that people will use.

6
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.500
You can pick a list that you already use, if you have one, or press

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.220
Add word and type your own.

8
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.360
Add the best answer first and the worst answer last.

9
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.120
Click any word to write what it means.

10
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.300
That sentence then goes to the Record.

11
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.820
If you leave a word's meaning empty, Quickler will write one for you shortly after.

12
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.520
The cross beside a word gets rid of it.

13
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.740
Or perhaps you'd rather a grade with a number.

14
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.520
Then in that case you can choose numbers and set the highest number.

15
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.720
On site, nobody will see this list.

16
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.180
They'll just say it in their own words and Quickler will pick the

17
00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.920
matching word, that is the matching grade.

18
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.960
You can open the key at the bottom of the Record to see every word

19
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:04.940
and what it means.

20
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.620
You can change a word's sentence here and it changes on every Record of that Check.

21
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:15.160
The key is printed on your PDF as well, so readers can see it too.

22
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.200
Or hide it by pressing Hide.

23
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.060
You can press it again to show it.
